#
# Give the bridge a liveness heartbeat. Every health check it had
# tested state a wedged daemon keeps - a live process, a listening
# socket - so a frozen or stuck bridge stayed Ready indefinitely while
# every request hung. The main loop now reports progress on every
# wakeup of every wait, with the longest that wait may legitimately
# block, and a publisher thread keeps a heartbeat file fresh only while
# the loop is within that bound. The two waits that could block forever
# are bounded so that an idle bridge still beats. See patches/README.md.
#
